clueweb09-enwp03-35-01488.0 The Man Who Invented the Moon From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search The Man Who Invented the Moon [] The Man Who Invented the Moon Directed by John Cabrera Produced by Larry Fitzgibbon Written by Lee Kirk Starring Sean Gunn Nicolette DiMaggio Julie Dolan Brent Sexton Music by Willie Wisely Cinematography Ken Seng Editing by John Cabrera Distributed by Normandie County Films Running time 32 mins Country [] United States Language English Official website ýýý IMDb The Man Who Invented the Moon is a 2003 film by Normandie County Films written by Lee Kirk and directed by John Cabrera. The film stars Sean Gunn, Nicolette DiMaggio, Julie Dolan, and Brent Sexton and was produced by Larry Fitzgibbon. The Man Who Invented the Moon was John Cabrera's directorial debut. Contents 1 Log Line 2 Cast 3 Festival Showings 4 References 5 External links [edit] Log Line Sammy Hughes
clueweb09-enwp03-35-01488.120 The Man Who Invented the Moon was John Cabrera's directorial debut. Contents 1 Log Line 2 Cast 3 Festival Showings 4 References 5 External links [edit] Log Line Sammy Hughes is famous. He's walked on the moon, trekked through Antarctica, dined with Abe Lincoln and Santa Claus... but now something very strange is about to happen to him. [edit] Cast Actor Role Sean Gunn Sammy Hughes Nicolette Dimaggio Haley/Megan Julie Dolan Haley 2 Brent Sexton Tommy Charles Brame Abe Lincoln Matt Gunn Dan McMahon Dave Barnes Santa Claus Eddie Ebell Jesus Christ Robert Gantzos Davy Crocket Michael Cornacchia Babe Ruth Michael Garvey Super Amazing Cathi Stinson Neighbor [edit] Festival Showings The Midwest Independent Film Festival Saint Louis International Film Festival Los Angeles International Short Film Festival [edit] References MWIFF 2006 Award Winners [edit] External links The Man Who Invented the Moon at the Internet Movie Database Official Site [] This
