clueweb09-enwp00-85-16075.0 Fickle, Indiana From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search Fickle [Fickle is located in Indiana] [Fickle] Fickle Coordinates: 40ýý15ýýý40ýýýN 86ýý40ýýý30ýýýWýýý / ýýý40.26111ýýN 86.675ýýWýýý / 40.26111; -86.675 Country United States State Indiana County Clinton Township Washington Elevation [1] 830 ft (253 m) ZIP code 46041 FIPS code 18-23134[2] GNIS feature ID 446766 Fickle is an unincorporated town in Washington Township, Clinton County, Indiana. [edit] Geography Fickle is located at 40ýý15ýýý40ýýýN 86ýý40ýýý30ýýýWýýý / ýýý40.26111ýýN 86.675ýýWýýý / 40.26111; -86.675. [edit] History The town of Fickle is named for Isaac Fickle, one of the early settlers of Washington Township. It was established as a station along the Toledo, St. Louis and Western Railroad, better known the "Clover Leaf" Railroad; the town's Clover Leaf Church is named for it.[3] [edit] References ^ "US Board on Geographic Names". United States Geological Survey. 25 October 2007. http://geonames.usgs.gov. Retrieved on 31 January 2008. ^ "American FactFinder".
